# MC-X-F6, undecided. L §4.4: "Equal intervals from different reads stay undecided", and so do overlapping ones; L
# §5.12 Sort: "An order that can't be decided (a hole) is refused (RUN-ORDER)"; L §8.4 RUN-ORDER `fill <f>: the order
# of <arc> is a hole`. Two lots dated by overlapping windows (2027-02-01 .. 2027-02-28, 2027-02-10 .. 2027-03-15):
# the fill's sort can't order them, and every take is refused (the arc named is the one the sort met).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source src "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind lots: event certain
index ids = [x1, x2]
input day[i in ids]: date
move lot[i in ids]: lots
  on day[i]
fill f
  supply 1 for l in lots over ..
  demand 1 for c in lots over ..
  arc true
  order l.day, c.day
version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2027-01-01
  day[x1] = window(2027-02-01, 2027-02-28)
  day[x2] = window(2027-02-10, 2027-03-15)
ask t: f.taken[l, c] for l in lots over .., c in lots over ..
=== expect
t (l = lot[x1], c = lot[x1]): refused: RUN-ORDER fill f: the order of the arc ...
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x1], c = lot[x2]): refused: RUN-ORDER fill f: the order of the arc ...
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x2], c = lot[x1]): refused: RUN-ORDER fill f: the order of the arc ...
  cut 2027-01-01
t (l = lot[x2], c = lot[x2]): refused: RUN-ORDER fill f: the order of the arc ...
  cut 2027-01-01
